  enough for you they include a band that  locks into a case and ties your wallet  to your phone which you can then  disconnect by unscrewing so you will be  guaranteed to never lose this wallet  personally i don't think that you need  it but it is a nice little extra for  those that worry about that now that's  not the only feature it also has a  built-in flap that you don't have to use  but you can if you want your cards to be  sealed in without any risk of those  falling out and on top of that there's  an adjustable rubber strap at the back  that can be used to give you a better  grip for your phone like one of the ring  things that people use with them and it  can also double as a little stand if  you're going to be watching videos on  your phone it can prop it up the  materials also feel premium and costing  less than half of what apple's while it  costs while being more secure this thing  is a no-brainer and we finally have  something that is ultra safe for those  of you guys that worry about losing the  wallet or your cards now if that's too  extreme for you they also make this  wallet which is way more minimalistic  but still high quality with strong  magnets and its standout feature is that  they use neoprene to hold your cards so  if you avoided max safe wallets because  they only had two or three card  capacities you can stuff five or more  into this one the material can stretch  to hold a lot of cards but don't worry  about them slipping out because the back  side is a really nice rubbery plastic  that grips your cards really well now  the magnets aren't as strong as the m  band but they are still stronger than  apples while being nice and slim and  costing only 15 to 18 bucks depending on  the color that you choose i'm glad that  we finally have some great unique and  secure wallets on the market now  compared to the cheap knockoffs that we  tested just about a year ago speaking of  knockoffs this one is really cool and  for a great price  this mac safe duo ripoff is just hitting  the market but instead of supporting two  devices it actually supports three now i  have been using this other duo copy for  a while now when traveling and it has  done a good job but just like apple's  expensive version it can't charge my  airpods on it while charging my phone  and my watch but this one actually gives  you  two cheap charging pads one on each side  of the watch so you can charge your air  pods your phone and the apple watch or  say two different smartphones as well  when it first launched people complained  about being flaky so they now include a  power adapter with it in the box that  can handle three devices unlike apple  where you have to buy that on your own  and it is only 38  the quality of this one is way better  than my previous one with rubber that  feels much like apple's versions and the  magnets are stronger as well when you  fold it it magnetizes together to itself  so it's very compact it's nice for  throwing in your bag taking with you and  even if you want to just use it as home  as an alternative to something else it's  really hard to beat at this price now of  course it won't give you full 15 watt  maxi charging speeds but it tops out at  the standard 7.5 watt g charging but  apple's duo also won't give you that  speed and that one also slows down more  if you're charging your watch at the  same time now if you want to step it up  a notch and you want something that will  not only give you the fastest charging  for your iphone but also your apple  watch as well this is belkin's new boost  up charge pro it's an upgrade to their  older three-in-one stand where your  phone and watch floats but in a slim  minimalistic package that can be easily  taken with you on the go you get the  benefit of knowing it is high quality  it's gonna last a long time and it's the  only other brand that apple actually  allows to use the full magsafe fast  charging and it's only one of three  chargers that can fast charge the 